2025-05-01 02:54:58 - Thread-1067 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables & columns for the task  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."ToUserId": receiver of an up‑vote → count distinct votes received per user.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."FromUserId": giver of an up‑vote → count distinct votes a user gave.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."Id": primary key, good for DISTINCT counting.  
• FORUMMESSAGEVOTES."VoteDate": can be used for optional date filters (none required now).  
• USERS."Id": joins to either ToUserId or FromUserId → maps user id → username.  
• USERS."UserName": the username we finally want to show.

Typical conditions that might be useful  
• "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL (and/or) "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL – ignore anonymous / missing votes.  
• COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") or COUNT(DISTINCT "FromUserId") – depending on the definition of “distinct”.  
• ORDER BY vote counts DESC, LIMIT 3 – keep only top three receivers.

Below are ten exploratory→complex Snowflake SQL snippets (each capped with LIMIT 20) to understand the data and finally retrieve the desired result.  All identifiers are double‑quoted to respect Snowflake case‑sensitivity.

```sql
--Description: Peek at a few vote records to understand basic values in ToUserId & FromUserId
SELECT "Id",
       "FromUserId",
       "ToUserId",
       "VoteDate"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: Show 20 different users who have received at least one vote
SELECT DISTINCT "ToUserId"
FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
WHERE  "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: Count how many total (non‑distinct) votes each receiver got; show top 20
SELECT   "ToUserId",
         COUNT(*)  AS "total_votes_received"
FROM     META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
WHERE    "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "ToUserId"
ORDER BY "total_votes_received" DESC
LIMIT    20;
```

```sql
--Description: Join receivers with USERS to get usernames for the 20 most‑voted users
SELECT   u."UserName",
         f."ToUserId",
         COUNT(*) AS "total_votes_received"
FROM     META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES f
JOIN     META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS            u
       ON u."Id" = f."ToUserId"
WHERE    f."ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY u."UserName", f."ToUserId"
ORDER BY "total_votes_received" DESC
LIMIT    20;
```

```sql
--Description: For one sample user, compare distinct up‑votes received vs given
SELECT
  f."ToUserId"  AS "UserId",
  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN f."ToUserId" = 638 THEN f."Id" END) AS "rec_votes",
  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN f."FromUserId" = 638 THEN f."Id" END) AS "sent_votes"
FROM META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES f
WHERE 638 IN (f."ToUserId", f."FromUserId")
GROUP BY f."ToUserId"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Build both counts (distinct vote rows) for every user that appears in votes
WITH base AS (
  SELECT "Id",
         "ToUserId",
         "FromUserId"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  WHERE  "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
)
SELECT
  COALESCE("ToUserId","FromUserId") AS "UserId",
  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN "ToUserId"  IS NOT NULL THEN "Id" END) AS "votes_received",
  COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL THEN "Id" END) AS "votes_given"
FROM base
GROUP BY COALESCE("ToUserId","FromUserId")
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Show users sorted by DISTINCT votes_received (row‑level distinctness)
WITH recv AS (
  SELECT "ToUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_received"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  WHERE  "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP  BY "ToUserId"
), sent AS (
  SELECT "FromUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_given"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  WHERE  "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP  BY "FromUserId"
)
SELECT r."UserId",
       r."votes_received",
       COALESCE(s."votes_given",0) AS "votes_given"
FROM   recv r
LEFT   JOIN sent s USING ("UserId")
ORDER  BY r."votes_received" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: Same as above but bring in username & keep only top 20 receivers
WITH recv AS (
  SELECT "ToUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_received"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  WHERE  "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP  BY "ToUserId"
), sent AS (
  SELECT "FromUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_given"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  WHERE  "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP  BY "FromUserId"
)
SELECT u."UserName",
       r."votes_received",
       COALESCE(s."votes_given",0) AS "votes_given"
FROM   recv r
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS u
      ON u."Id" = r."UserId"
LEFT  JOIN sent s USING ("UserId")
ORDER  BY r."votes_received" DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
--Description: Capture exactly the TOP 3 users with most distinct votes received
WITH recv AS (
  SELECT "ToUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_received"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  WHERE  "ToUserId" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP  BY "ToUserId"
), sent AS (
  SELECT "FromUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_given"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  WHERE  "FromUserId" IS NOT NULL
  GROUP  BY "FromUserId"
), ranked AS (
  SELECT r."UserId",
         r."votes_received",
         COALESCE(s."votes_given",0) AS "votes_given",
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY r."votes_received" DESC) AS rn
  FROM   recv r
  LEFT   JOIN sent s USING ("UserId")
)
SELECT u."UserName",
       ranked."votes_received",
       ranked."votes_given"
FROM   ranked
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS u
      ON u."Id" = ranked."UserId"
WHERE  ranked.rn <= 3
ORDER  BY ranked."votes_received" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: Same final logic but using QUALIFY instead of outer query; still limited
WITH recv AS (
  SELECT "ToUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_received"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  GROUP  BY "ToUserId"
), sent AS (
  SELECT "FromUserId" AS "UserId",
         COUNT(DISTINCT "Id") AS "votes_given"
  FROM   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.FORUMMESSAGEVOTES
  GROUP  BY "FromUserId"
)
SELECT u."UserName",
       r."votes_received",
       COALESCE(s."votes_given",0) AS "votes_given"
FROM   recv r
JOIN   META_KAGGLE.META_KAGGLE.USERS u
       ON u."Id" = r."UserId"
LEFT  JOIN sent s USING ("UserId")
QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY r."votes_received" DESC) <= 3
LIMIT 20;
```
